.pio
.vscode/.browse.c_cpp.db*
.vscode/c_cpp_properties.json
.vscode/launch.json
.vscode/ipch

# The database of what each file includes, written for the language server of an editor: it is
# generated from the build and not source —the flags are the ones in `platformio.ini`— and it is
# different in every machine, so the repository does not keep it.
compile_commands.json

# The disk an environment is flashed with: `tools/make_disk.py` puts `data/` and,
# on a board with room, `apps/` together in here. It is generated, not source, and
# it is the same in every run (docs/80).
build/

# Working disk of the emulator: it is state, not code.
emulator/

# The card in the slot of the emulated board is a directory of somebody's data, always the same one.
emulator/sd/

# What an app writes when the emulator runs (the `data/` of the assembled disk): the app data
# area of the emulated flash. The code is `apps/` and `data/res`; this is a run.
data/data/

# The pages `http` saved when they did not fit in memory: a download is somebody's file and not code.
data/http/

# Leftovers of an older layout, kept next to the repository and never built.
OLD/
DevelNotes.md
